{
  "iri": "https://strandz.it/jigdaw/plugins/markov/",
  "label": "Markov",
  "comment": "Markov-chain melody generator: a random walk over the twelve pitch classes driven by a 12 by 12 transition matrix, filled by one of eight styles or learned from a melodic line on its MIDI input, and played in time with the host transport.",
  "vendor": "danja",
  "developer": "http://danny.ayers.name",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "format": "trn:Jig , trn:WebAudio",
  "licenceId": "MIT",
  "prefers": [],
  "registeredName": "markov",
  "roles": [
    "trn:MidiGenerator"
  ],
  "accepts": [
    "trn:Midi",
    "trn:ControlMidi"
  ],
  "produces": [
    "trn:Midi",
    "trn:MelodyMidi"
  ],
  "cautions": [
    "Silent until the host transport is rolling and reports a tempo and a beat position. Pure MIDI, no audio: route its MIDI output to an instrument. Ported from the Downspout VST3 of the same name; the status read-outs and the panel are not carried over, and the random draw is the VST3's 64-bit mix.",
    "The matrix is set by Style and Randomise, or learned. The VST3's cell-by-cell matrix editor is not carried over. The matrix and what it has learned are the plugin's saved state, so a reopened session plays the same melody.",
    "Declares no jig:module and so no jig:abi. A host that loads a module directly, such as the native adapter, cannot load this plugin; a JavaScript AudioWorklet host can."
  ],
  "requires": [
    "jig:MidiEvents",
    "jig:MidiOut",
    "trn:HostTransport"
  ],
  "shape": {
    "audioInputs": 0,
    "audioOutputs": 0,
    "renderQuantum": 128,
    "latencyFrames": 0
  },
  "resources": {
    "processor": "markov-processor.js"
  },
